        "original_id": "e1f4f318-239b-51ea-b9f5-50797e02de57",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Delilah Rene, Martin Block, Alan Freed, Dick Clark, Ameen Sayani, Wolfman Jack, Casey Kasem, Don Imus, Howard Stern, Mike Francesa, Rush Limbaugh, Skip Kelly, Ryan Seacrest, Danny Bonaduce, Matt Siegel, Dale Dorman, Dave Kutch, Sarah McLachlan\n- Roles: Radio personalities, pop music radio hosts, shock jocks, sports talk hosts, political talk hosts, producer, remastering engineer, author, songwriter\n- Products: Live Acoustic\n\nFacts:\n- Delilah Rene was born on February 15, 1960, in North Bend, Oregon.\n- Delilah Rene is an American radio personality, author, and songwriter.\n- Delilah Rene is best known as the host of a nationally syndicated nightly U.S. radio song request and dedication program with an estimated 8 million listeners.\n- Notable radio personalities include pop music radio hosts Martin Block, Alan Freed, Dick Clark, Delilah, Ameen Sayani, Wolfman Jack, and Casey Kasem.\n- Notable radio personalities also include shock jocks Don Imus and Howard Stern, sports talk host Mike Francesa, and political talk host Rush Limbaugh.\n- Skip Kelly has shared the mic on air with Ryan Seacrest, Danny Bonaduce, Delilah, Matt Siegel, and Dale Dorman.\n- The tracks on Sarah McLachlan's EP Live Acoustic were produced by Skip Kelly and remastered by Dave Kutch.",
